`JsonSerializer.isEmpty(SerializerProvider, T)` is now `isEmptyValue` everywhere in the repository, and the build passes.

`./mvnw test` ran 3895 tests with 0 failures, plus the 3 type-pollution tests (1 skipped, as before). It ran from this checkout's own `pom.xml` and compiled this checkout's sources.

I took the 54 edit sites from the compiler-backed `prism change-impact` run and renamed only those lines. They cover:
- the declaration in `JsonSerializer`;
- every serializer override in `main`, including the XML, SQL Blob, array, map, reference, delegating and value serializers;
- the two test overrides, in `TestEmptyClass` and `JsonInclude4464Test`;
- every call on a serializer, including the self-call at `JsonSerializer.java:208`.

I also updated two comments that referred to the old name: the `{@link}` in `JsonSerializer`'s deprecation note, and the commented-out signature in `ContainerSerializer`.

I left the deprecated one-argument `isEmpty(T)`, `JsonSerializable.isEmpty(SerializerProvider)` and all other `isEmpty` methods alone. The diff also shows `CLAUDE.md`, which was already modified before I started.
